<include>
  <!--
    Pipecat demo dialplan (context "mrf" — where the pipecat SIP profile lands calls).

    5000 -> the AI bot. drachtio mod_audio_fork (MIT) streams the caller's audio
    (binary L16 @ 8 kHz) to the Pipecat bot over a WebSocket.

       uuid_audio_fork <uuid> start ws://192.168.0.16:7860/audio mono 8k

    WS URL = the Windows host LAN IP where the bot listens (bot stays on Windows). With
    WSL2 mirrored networking, FreeSWITCH-in-WSL reaches the Windows bot at this address.
    CHANGE 192.168.0.16 to your host LAN IP (`ipconfig`) if it differs.

    ====================================================================================
    STATUS (2026-07-23): CAPTURE works (caller -> STT -> LLM -> flow, verified). PLAYBACK
    (bot -> caller) DOES NOT WORK with this image's mod_audio_fork build, and is the one
    open item. Root cause is understood; the exact enable-incantation is not.

    Findings (from binary `strings` of the image's mod_audio_fork.so, since no matching
    public source exists — davehorton's repo 404s; mdslaney/dochong clones are older and
    lack this feature):
      * This build DOES support bidirectional playback — two modes:
          - playAudio JSON  -> temp file (.r16/.wav) -> broadcast into channel
          - raw BINARY back -> real-time inject via SWITCH_ABC_TYPE_WRITE_REPLACE
        Both are OFF BY DEFAULT. Inbound binary is dropped with
        "received unexpected binary frame, discarding" until stream mode is enabled.
      * The API usage string lists enabling args:
          <uuid> start <url> [mono|mixed|stereo] [8000..] [bugname] [metadata]
                 [bidirectionalAudio_enabled] [bidirectionalAudio_stream_enabled]
                 [bidirectionalAudio_stream_samplerate]
      * Verified via an automated harness (FS originates a SIP call into 5000, records
        what the caller hears, measures level; native-playback control on 5001 PASSES,
        so the harness is sound). None of these enabled playback:
          positional `0 1 8000`, `1 1 8000`, `true true 8000`, JSON `{}` metadata,
          `8k` vs `8000` rate, the `audio.drachtio.org` subprotocol on the peer,
          and channel vars bidirectional_audio_(enable|stream_enable|sample_rate).
      * Earlier "mixed"/"stereo" broke capture too; that was the parked-leg no-write-cycle
        issue (send_silence_when_idle fixed capture but not playback).

    Reliable paths forward (pick per the bigger prod-architecture decision):
      (a) Get the enable syntax from the drachtio/jambonz author or a jambonz deployment
          (jambonz uses this exact build for two-way audio in production).
      (b) Bypass mod_audio_fork playback: native FS `uuid_broadcast`/`playback` driven
          over ESL from the bot (native playback is PROVEN here — the 5001 control).
      (c) Revert playback to amigniter mod_audio_stream (real-time streamAudio inject,
          works with a Pipecat bot; free tier <=10 concurrent — a prod-scale licensing
          decision, not a dev blocker).
    ====================================================================================

    7000 -> answer + park (no fork). 5001 -> native tone playback (harness control).
    Reload after edits:  docker exec pcfs-freeswitch fs_cli -x reloadxml
  -->
  <context name="mrf">
    <extension name="pipecat-bot">
      <condition field="destination_number" expression="^5000$">
        <action application="answer"/>
        <!-- send_silence_when_idle gives the channel a continuous outbound write-frame
             cycle for mod_audio_fork's WRITE_REPLACE to inject bot audio into (without it,
             a parked leg has no write frames and playback is silent). -->
        <action application="set" data="send_silence_when_idle=-1"/>
        <!-- jambonz PIPE-delimited (^^|) invocation, bidirectional binary STREAMING on.
             Fields: uuid|start|url|mix|sampling|bugname|metadata|enabled|streaming|rate.
             enabled=true streaming=true rate=8000 -> bot sends raw L16 binary frames,
             module injects them in real time. (Space-delimited args do NOT enable this.) -->
        <!-- ?uuid=${uuid} lets the bot learn the channel UUID so it can hang the call up
             over ESL at end-of-flow (uuid_kill); without it the caller stays parked. -->
        <action application="set" data="stream=${uuid_audio_fork(^^|${uuid}|start|ws://192.168.0.16:7860/audio?uuid=${uuid}|mono|8000|||true|true|8000)}"/>
        <action application="park"/>
      </condition>
    </extension>
    <extension name="parked-test-leg">
      <condition field="destination_number" expression="^7000$">
        <action application="answer"/>
        <action application="park"/>
      </condition>
    </extension>
    <!-- Harness control: native FS playback of a 480Hz tone (no fork). Proves the
         record-and-measure harness detects channel-write audio. -->
    <extension name="control-playback-tone">
      <condition field="destination_number" expression="^5001$">
        <action application="answer"/>
        <action application="playback" data="tone_stream://%(60000,0,480)"/>
      </condition>
    </extension>
    <!-- TEST (5003): fork to tone WS server (7862) with jambonz's PIPE-delimited (^^|)
         invocation, bidirectional binary STREAMING on (enabled|streaming|rate = true|true|8000).
         Fields: uuid|start|url|mix|sampling|bugname|metadata|enabled|streaming|rate. -->
    <extension name="stream-inject-test">
      <condition field="destination_number" expression="^5003$">
        <action application="answer"/>
        <action application="set" data="send_silence_when_idle=-1"/>
        <action application="set" data="stream=${uuid_audio_fork(^^|${uuid}|start|ws://192.168.0.16:7862/audio|mono|8000|||true|true|8000)}"/>
        <action application="park"/>
      </condition>
    </extension>
  </context>
</include>
